  "label": "Single Cell Spatial Integration Methods",
  "related": [
    "inference-gene-4e7e",
    "untitled-topic-53a8",
    "transcriptomics-single-ab11"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "untitled-topic-1773",
  "summary": "Single-cell and spatial datasets increasingly span chromatin, expression, spatial, and perturbation modalities, demanding scalable integration.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational inference of regulatory and spatial organization by integrating heterogeneous single-cell and spatial measurements. Cis-TERN couples scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq via network diffusion on a directed bipartite graph to infer pseudotime, while scGALA and CelLink align cells across datasets, CelLink handling weak feature linkage and imbalanced populations with iterative optimal transport. Spatial work spans continuous spatiotemporal dynamics in STODE, per-gene gradients in SLOPER, missing-tissue reconstruction in MIMYR, and language-model generation in TissueNarrator. TNDE and scDRP extend this to time-varying regulatory and perturbation effects estimated from snapshot data, and scMRDR integrates unpaired single-cell and spatial multi-omics. What is new is the breadth of modality bridging across chromatin accessibility, expression, spatial, and perturbation data within generative and graph-based frameworks. Not every item shares this thread; virtual-cell simulators such as VCWorld and CellTRIP extend it toward perturbation prediction.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-30"
}
